#    CindersLauncher.exe from the game's folder, the folder above it (the Unity player sits in unity/) or HKCU\Software\CindersOfChaos
#    \InstallDir, then main() returns. prepareRestart() gives the next process its own 60 s ticket (Application::relaunchIfRequested
#    starts the new client after an update, base patch 0101), so a restart needs no launcher.
#  * src/client/CMakeLists.txt: option CHAOS_REQUIRE_LAUNCHER (default OFF) -> -DCHAOS_REQUIRE_LAUNCHER=1. Everything is compiled
#    out without it: Android (a phone has no launcher), Linux and every development build never see the check. The Windows release
#    workflows pass ON.
# A deterrent, not security: the key is in every client and launcher, only obfuscated; whoever patches the exe skips the check.
# Not built against the real client tree (the base is not in the repository): the headers pass the C++ tests here (the platform half
# on Linux only: its Windows branch was never compiled), the hunks were dry-run on files rebuilt from the context of 0035, 0101, 0102
